  "summary": "Scaled domain and architecture annotation across defined taxon sets now yields quantitative catalogues of phage and defense system diversity.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is large-scale computational enumeration of sequence and domain diversity within defined taxon sets, reported as catalogues or newly defined classes. The eCIS survey annotates 3445 tail fiber proteins from 1069 prokaryotes, defining five new N-terminal receptor-binding domains and 276 structural clusters. The BREX study maps BREX domains across comparative genomes, defining three new BREX-related defense subtypes and a composite anti-phage system. A k-mer Jaccard pangenome analysis of 3384 U.S. Salmonella Hadar genomes documents a 2019-2020 lineage shift linked to poultry spread, while PhageMind applies meta-learning over a knowledge graph of tail fibers and O-antigen gene clusters to predict strain-level host range. What is new is the scale of domain and architecture annotation applied to defined sets, with the eCIS and BREX studies contributing explicit enumerations of previously undescribed domains and subtypes.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-01-28"
}
